2025-11-27 08:09:59,831 - benchmark.results_formatter - INFO -       Task Fulfillment:
2025-11-27 08:09:59,831 - benchmark.results_formatter - INFO -         The agent identified key subtasks—dataset searches for BRAF‐targeted trials, PubMed abstracts, TCGA survival data, and ClinVar variant information—and provided an executive summary on mutation prevalence, therapy shifts, and outcomes. However, it never pulled quantitative trial counts or survival curves directly from any tool, and variant frequencies were not extracted from ClinVar. It addressed ~75% of the concrete requirements (discovery of datasets and high-level synthesis but missing direct data extraction and analysis).
2025-11-27 08:09:59,831 - benchmark.results_formatter - INFO -       Grounding:
2025-11-27 08:09:59,831 - benchmark.results_formatter - INFO -         While the summary cites credible repositories (e.g. irds/clinicaltrials_2019, cyberpsych PubMed NLP, rosenthal/tcga-path-notes, songlab/clinvar), none of the key numerical claims (40–50% prevalence, PFS gains, resistance timelines) are directly anchored to tool outputs or exact dataset queries. Roughly half of the substantive claims are supported only by literature convention rather than extracted evidence.
2025-11-27 08:09:59,831 - benchmark.results_formatter - INFO -       Tool Appropriateness:
2025-11-27 08:09:59,832 - benchmark.results_formatter - INFO -         The agent largely used Hugging Face dataset and model searches for each subtask, which is appropriate for locating data resources. But it over-applied search-spaces and search-models for clinical-trial and mutation queries where those tools yielded no relevant items, indicating ~50% of selected tools were optimal.
2025-11-27 08:09:59,832 - benchmark.results_formatter - INFO -       Parameter Accuracy:
2025-11-27 08:09:59,832 - benchmark.results_formatter - INFO -         All 40 Hugging Face calls used syntactically correct parameters (query strings, limits) and none failed due to malformed arguments. Though many queries returned no hits, their parameters matched expected API usage, giving ~85–90% accuracy.
2025-11-27 08:09:59,832 - benchmark.results_formatter - INFO -       Dependency Awareness:
2025-11-27 08:09:59,854 - benchmark.results_formatter - INFO -         The agent roughly followed the intended chain—literature search → variant data → clinical trial identification → outcome analysis—but mixed steps (e.g. searching models/spaces midstream) and never fully executed the final analysis. It handled about 60% of dependencies in the correct order.
2025-11-27 08:09:59,855 - benchmark.results_formatter - INFO -       Parallelism & Efficiency:
2025-11-27 08:09:59,855 - benchmark.results_formatter - INFO -         All tool calls were issued serially, often repeating similar dataset searches (e.g. multiple melanoma/dabrafenib queries) with no batching or parallel execution. Redundancy in queries was high, indicating under 30% efficiency.
